*- [EPIC] [TI-0095] Deferred platform and collaboration capabilities
  [DESC] Revisit these capabilities only after the local single-user post-processing workflow is proven.

    #- [FT] [TI-0096] Add live transcription after post-processing stabilizes
      [DESC] Added an on-device provisional preview from recoverable microphone and system chunks; native recording validation remains.
      [DESC] Native test evidence (Sep 20, 2026, meeting "test1"): preview updates stopped after the first intervals; leaving Record for Settings or Meetings discarded already captured preview text and returned to "Listening for speech".
      [DESC] Native test evidence: at 05:00 the preview invented repetitive microphone and meeting-audio phrases that were not spoken, including repeated "If you are able to do it" and "All right" text.
      [DESC] Native test evidence: the GTK shell became unresponsive around 07:38 while live preview inference was running. The preview command synchronously ran FFmpeg and Whisper over growing chunks, blocking desktop command handling.
      [DESC] Interruption evidence: "test1" remained in recording state after the crash although its recording directory preserved 20 microphone, raw-microphone, and system WAV chunks; its incomplete manifest exposed no recovery/transcription action in the library.
      [DESC] Recovery verification exposed a second-interruption defect: fixed idempotency keys replayed the first recovery transition and could leave a later interrupted transcription stranded in processing; recovery keys now include the meeting revision.
      [DESC] Acceptance: bound preview work to short windows off the command thread, retain preview lines across navigation, suppress low-energy/repetitive hallucinations, and automatically expose interrupted audio for playback and final transcription.
      [DESC] Implemented bounded 15-second preview windows on blocking workers, session-owned navigation-safe preview state, PCM speech-energy gating, repeated-phrase rejection, asynchronous final transcription, and revision-safe interrupted-job recovery.
      [DESC] Verified with the preserved test1 audio (expected opening sentence in 2.88 seconds), 29 Rust tests, Clippy with warnings denied, frontend tests/build, SQLite integrity, and a native recovery launch; a fresh multi-minute recording remains for native acceptance.
      [DESC] Native retest evidence (Sep 20, 2026, meeting "test2"): live transcription still needs lower latency and improved draft accuracy; the interface should explicitly explain that live text is provisional and final transcription is reprocessed after recording.
      [DESC] Code review found each one-minute chunk capped at preview window index 3, causing the same 15-second slice to be reprocessed after 45 seconds until chunk rotation; microphone and system previews also run sequentially and can display duplicated bleed.
      [DESC] Replaced the capped windows with continuing non-overlapping eight-second windows, reduced the post-update delay from five to 2.5 seconds, prioritized the system pass, added fuzzy same-window live bleed suppression, identified original versus echo-reduced microphone labels, and added a visible provisional accuracy/delay warning.
      [DESC] On preserved test2 audio, an eight-second Fast-model system pass took 1.60 seconds and the microphone pass took 1.81 seconds (approximately 5-6 seconds per two-track refresh including delay). Verified continuing windows beyond 45 seconds, imperfect short-window bleed matching, 39 Rust tests, warning-free Clippy, frontend tests, structure checks, and the production build; a native multi-minute acceptance retest remains.
      [DESC] Native retest evidence (Sep 20, 2026, screencast at /home/jihadali/Videos/Screencasts/Screencast from 20-09-26 07:57:30 PM IST.webm): meeting "test3" reaches 2:10 while the visible live transcript remains at 0:00, 0:08, and 0:16 and the header repeatedly shows "Updating locally".
      [DESC] The test3 capture preserved 3m 40s across four synchronized chunks. Direct Fast-model replay successfully transcribed later system windows at 0:32, 0:40, and 0:48, isolating the observed failure to stale/clipped presentation rather than capture or Whisper inference.
      [DESC] Acceptance: keep the newest live passages visible, expose the latest audio timestamp checked even when a window yields no text, and distinguish active processing from a caught-up preview.
      [DESC] Implemented checkedThroughMs progress from the latest readable chunk, newest-three passage rendering with retained-history count, caught-up/processing/delayed status labels, a 20-second lag warning, and a no-clear-speech state that still reports checked audio progress.
      [DESC] Verified later test3 windows directly with the installed Fast model, 40 Rust tests, four frontend tests, warning-free Clippy, repository structure checks, and the production build; native visual acceptance remains.
